by the linearity of expectation. Since $u_{l} \sim \text{Unif}(-10,10)$ we have $E[u_{l]} = \frac{10 + (-10)}{2} = 0$ and since $u_{w} \sim \text{Unif}(-5,10)$ we have $E[u_{w]} = \frac{10 + (-5)}{2} = 2.5$. Finally, since $u_{l}$ and $u_{w}$ are independent, we have, $E[u_{w]}E[u_{l]} = E[u_{w]}E[u_{l]} = 0 \times 2.5 = 0$. Thus, the expected area is,
